+ * _TIME_BITS=64 - directly, or via a toolchain/distro default, or because
+ * somebody later adds it as a "portability" flag.  Every struct below then
+ * grows by 4 bytes (measured), the build still succeeds with no diagnostic
+ * whatsoever, and the protocol silently desynchronises from the client while
+ * the DB rows silently shift.  src/Makefile therefore never defines
+ * _TIME_BITS=64; these assertions are the tripwire in case that changes.
+ * (-D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 on its own is safe - it does not widen time_t.)
